WEBVTT

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:03.300
My passionate Idol Activities,

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:06.350
Aikatsu! is about to start!

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:10.560
My name is Hoshimiya Ichigo.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:15.460
I'm a first-year student aiming to be a top idol just like Kanzaki Mizuki-chan.

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:19.040
Right now I'm giving my all at the idol training school, Starlight Academy,

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.540
to live an Aikatsu life that everyone will admire!

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:27.040
Aikatsu stands for "idol activities", which include applying for auditions and getting gigs.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:31.000
We use Aikatsu cards to choose our own outfits and stages.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.140
This girl's name is Arisugawa Otome-chan.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:37.300
She may have failed the Special Christmas Event audition,

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.900
but there's still the Revenge Audition coming up.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:43.200
If she passes, then Aoi, Ran, Otome-chan and I

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.020
will be in the Christmas event together.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:46.960
Otome-chan, go for it!

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:05.320
Hi, signalize!

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:10.660
The answer lies on the other side of the sky

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:10.660
kotae wa motto takai sora no kanata

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.550
No, that's wrong

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.550
iie chigau yo

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:17.930
I can see with my eyes that it's at the end of the Earth

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:17.930
boku no me ni mo mieta chi no hate

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:19.720
Do that signalize!

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:24.900
Something's starting to bubble up

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:24.900
hageshiku natta mune no atsui powaa

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:28.860
From the burning power in my raging heart

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:28.860
sou da minagiru nanika ga

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:32.400
So I'll believe in the present

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:32.400
dakara ima wo shinjite

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:37.570
And start today since it's more than a faint desire

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:37.570
hajimeyou tada no akogare ja nai

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:38.910
Chance for me

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:44.210
Dreams can make even the harshest nightmare pleasant

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:44.210
zankoku na yume ga yume de yume ni narunda

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:48.420
It's just another challenge on the way

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:48.420
hora chousen matteru yo

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:53.340
Where are we headed?

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:53.340
kimi to mukau basho wa doko darou

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:57.090
Into a brilliant hope

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:57.090
mabushii kibou no naka e

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:04.350
Where do we want to go? Let's go find it right now

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:04.350
nozomu basho wa doko darou sagashi ni ikou yo shuppatsu da

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:07.730
Where we're headed

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:07.730
mukau basho wa mirai no

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.610
is into our hopes for the future

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.610
bokura no kibou no naka ni

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:18.950
Our destination is the future, the light is our signal Let's go, go!

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:18.950
nozomu basho wa mirai no kagayaki ga aizu let's go, go

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:31.040
Otome-chan, let's all train together for your Revenge Audition.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:33.040
Aye! I'll do my best!

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:36.040
Here's the special Aikatsu training menu I made.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:38.820
You're always reliable, Aoi!

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:39.800
Nicely done!

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:44.300
It was nothing at all. I threw it together for the sake of performing together on Christmas.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:49.300
Stage walking is pretty basic, and Otome-chan's been doing this much longer than us,

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.500
so shouldn't we skip it?

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.800
The basics are important. 
They're the foundation.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:56.800
Those who laugh away the basics are sure to cry.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:00.740
That's right. Ran, are you going to do the special training with us?

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:03.380
I'll take care of things myself.

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:07.740
Don't you think that it's better to just let 
people train how they want to?

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:10.800
What? But it's Otome-chan we're talking about.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:14.220
We just became friends, so I want to do something together with everyone.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:16.540
It's great you feel that way,

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.260
but Otome seems to have left.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:21.260
Huh? Where'd she go?

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:24.300
I even made this training menu for her...

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:29.580
Otome-chan!

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:33.800
You two are helpless...

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:41.000
What are you doing up there, Otome-chan?

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.030
Love you.

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:49.800
Is she trying to save the kitten that got stuck up in the tree?

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:51.460
Oh no!

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:09.100
Love you!

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.780
Unlike you, the cat can get down by itself.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:18.600
Stand up.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:24.340
I'm moved! Thanksies!

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:26.880
Please don't make my work any harder.

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:31.260
That sure was scary.

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:34.220
If the groundskeeper hadn't been there, you could've gotten hurt.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:35.620
Thank goodness you're safe.

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:37.740
Yep, I'm fine.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:54.060
Otome-chan!

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:54.820
Yes?

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.360
Let's do the dance lesson together.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:58.600
It'll be fun.

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:01.360
Ichigo, it's not all fun and games.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:06.280
If you don't stay aware of your center of mass, then you won't be able to dance properly.

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:09.360
Otome-chan, what's wrong? Let's practice.

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:11.440
My heart is pounding!

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:13.340
Love you, you!

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:17.340
N-No way...

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:20.580
Did Otome-chan fall in love with the groundskeeping guy?

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:26.400
Have you any injuries?

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:29.240
My Princess.

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:36.780
Love! So this is love!

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:39.720
What should we do?

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:47.240
So what do you expect me to do?

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:48.820
Don't you have experience?

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:50.760
Experience?

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:52.920
About the feeling of being a girl in love.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:56.080
H-How would I know about that?

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:57.560
Oh...

00:05:57.560 --> 00:05:59.600
Then what about you?

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:00.580
Nope.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:04.160
Even if you ask me about love, nothing quite comes to mind.

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:06.580
All I've got is that guys are simple-minded.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:09.480
That's right.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:12.680
They try to figure out how many people they can stuff into a garbage dump,

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:17.660
and say "Hey, Hoshimiya. Do this and try to say 'school library' out loud", and stuff.

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:18.720
Shool lai—

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:20.000
Stop there.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:21.980
I understand...

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:24.220
Aoi, nothing comes to mind, right?

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:26.460
I do understand... a bit.

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:27.480
Huh?!

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:30.620
So you had a boy that you liked?

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:33.700
Who, who? Do I know him?

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.640
Probably not.

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:39.000
We went to the same cram school.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.500
He was a pretty normal guy.

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:46.180
We talked and messed around a bit, but I didn't really think twice about him. {fuck all of you people who keep reposting this}

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.940
Until that one autumn evening.

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:54.040
I passed by him on the way home from school.

00:06:56.900 --> 00:07:01.230
The fading sunlight stained his hair a beautiful gold.

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:04.040
He was really handsome.

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:07.780
After that I became more aware of him.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:11.300
But one month later,

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:13.700
his family moved away.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:15.600
A tragic love, indeed.

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:21.360
Yet during that one short month, everything around me seemed so wonderful.

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:24.620
The dancing leaves upon the sidewalk,

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:26.700
the chilly winds running through my hair,

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:28.860
and the slow lengthening of my shadow...

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:48.000
How nice! I want to fall in love like that!

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:50.640
Hey, I'm not saying it was love or anything.

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:54.540
I wonder if Otome-chan is living within a sparkling daydream like that too.

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:59.020
I'm not sure about that, but I've heard that romance has a positive effect on your skin.

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:02.640
When you're in love, estrogen is made inside your head,

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:04.980
and it gets rid of dull and dry skin!

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:09.540
Moreover, if your head is full of thoughts about him, you might not be able to eat as much.

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:11.740
The hunger center in your brain gets suppressed

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:13.760
and you'll get similar results to being on a diet.

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:16.680
Wow! Love is amazing!

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:18.780
Alright! Time to find love!

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:21.220
I want to have a fantastic love too.

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:24.780
Aren't you forgetting something fundamental here?

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:26.650
Something fundamental?

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:29.020
Romance is forbidden for idols.

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:32.520
I forgot!

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:34.560
But why?

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:36.900
Idols are for everyone to admire.

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:39.540
They mustn't belong to just a single person.

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:42.220
For everyone to admire...

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:43.560
I see.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:47.780
Romance is forbidden for idols, huh.

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:51.280
No matter how in love Otome-chan is, she can't consummate it.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:58.260
Love you.

00:08:58.260 --> 00:08:59.760
Cheer up.

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:00.700
That's right.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:03.340
Aye! I'm super happy!

00:09:03.340 --> 00:09:04.780
You're in love, right?

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:07.260
Love? Not really.

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:11.100
But your heart was pounding and you couldn't focus on practice.

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:15.780
That person is all you can think about, and you can't eat or drink anything.

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:17.640
"That person"?

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:21.080
Oh! Today's lunch was delicious.

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:23.780
I had penne arrabiata again.

00:09:23.780 --> 00:09:25.340
It was a bit spicy!

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:30.290
Did you know that romance is forbidden for idols?

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:34.820
Yeah. But I just can't hold back this excitement!

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:36.160
Alright then!

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:39.200
We'll support you, okay?

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:40.800
Y-Yeah.

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:43.400
It's fine if romance is forbidden for idols.

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:46.860
We're your friends, so we'll cheer you on.

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:49.800
But I don't even know the name.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:51.220
Name?

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:53.620
His name is...

00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:54.600
Name?

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:55.620
I don't know.

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:57.840
What?! Not even <i>you</i> know?

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:01.720
The two of us don't know anything about him either.

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:05.420
Okay! Time for Special Operation: 
Research the groundskeeping guy!

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:06.840
Yeah!

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:10.380
The groundskeeping guy?

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:30.860
One of his jobs is tending the flower beds.

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:38.380
He's passionately and briskly completing his job, and he's very skilled.

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:46.600
Naoto, good job as usual.

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:47.920
Hear that?

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:50.280
You bet I heard! What great info.

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:52.080
His first name is Naoto.

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:53.980
I'm about finished here.

00:10:53.980 --> 00:10:55.860
Yeah, nicely done.

00:10:59.440 --> 00:11:00.880
There's an audition.

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:04.300
That's right! I-It's the...

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:06.080
Cleaning Girl audition!

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:08.380
It's the Special Operation audition!

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:10.900
Was there really an audition like that?

00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:13.920
Please give us permission to leave school grounds!

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:15.920
Nothing Problem!

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:16.900
Bepp!

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:44.020
Huh? Where'd he go?

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:45.980
Let's split up and search.

00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:49.600
Got it. I'll call you via Aikatsu phone if I find him.

00:12:07.020 --> 00:12:08.860
I wonder where he went?

00:12:55.220 --> 00:12:56.360
Hey, you!

00:12:56.560 --> 00:12:58.360
You aren't allowed to hold concerts here!

00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:00.600
Crap! Hey, Hoshimiya!

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:02.320
Help us!

00:13:03.140 --> 00:13:04.100
Hurry up already.

00:13:14.740 --> 00:13:16.480
Thanks for the help, Hoshimiya.

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:19.160
Not a problem, it was fun.

00:13:19.160 --> 00:13:22.460
Huh? Why do you know my name?

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:25.260
I'm Suzukawa Naoto.

00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:25.940
The groundskeeper.

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:34.860
Ah! The groundskeeping guy!

00:13:36.180 --> 00:13:38.940
Looks like she's caught Nao the groundskeeper.

00:13:38.940 --> 00:13:40.960
I didn't know you were in a band.

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:44.660
We've still got a long way to go.

00:13:44.660 --> 00:13:46.760
Get it? We're More Than Tr—

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:50.700
We started as a roadside band.

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:53.460
That's why we do these guerilla concerts once in a while.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:55.980
I get it now.

00:13:56.360 --> 00:13:58.180
He's the guitarist, Hiro.

00:13:58.180 --> 00:13:59.400
Hey there.

00:13:59.680 --> 00:14:01.300
The bassist Shurato.

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:06.300
We've also got a drummer called King,

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:09.240
but drums are heavy and hard to run away with.

00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:11.160
Now then, Hoshimiya...

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:13.020
See you at the studio.

00:14:13.020 --> 00:14:15.000
Don't go making girls cry, now.

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:16.000
Shut it!

00:14:17.780 --> 00:14:19.900
How about you tell me something?

00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:23.420
You've been following me around all day, right?

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:28.760
Um, I had to make an observation diary of you for my homework.

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:31.260
That's a lie.

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:34.900
A-Actually, I was thinking that your job looked really tough,

00:14:34.900 --> 00:14:36.740
so I was wondering exactly what you did.

00:14:38.360 --> 00:14:42.500
I lost an important accessory, and I thought you might know about it.

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:45.520
I'm starting a fan club!

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:49.020
It's a secret society's conspiracy...

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:58.740
I'm sorry. The truth is...

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:02.440
One of my friends seems to really like you.

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:03.760
Huh?

00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:05.420
And so, that's why I...

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:10.140
She's a close friend of mine, so I thought I would do some research about you for her.

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:16.310
I understand.

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:20.440
But I'm not interested in any of the girls at the school.

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:21.920
You're all just kids to me.

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:25.160
Just kids...

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:27.800
That's too bad.

00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:32.820
Well, at least I'll admit that there are people who will go out of their way to help a friend in need.

00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:38.780
I'm happy about her feelings,

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:41.460
but tell your friend that I can't accept them.

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:42.300
Okay.

00:15:42.640 --> 00:15:44.160
One more thing—

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:47.380
Don't tell anyone that I'm in a band.

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:49.340
Sure, I won't tell a soul.

00:16:03.320 --> 00:16:06.360
Oh no! I forgot to call Aoi!

00:16:10.020 --> 00:16:12.020
Otome-chan, do you understand?

00:16:12.020 --> 00:16:14.020
Yeah, I understand.

00:16:14.020 --> 00:16:15.020
It's too bad,

00:16:15.520 --> 00:16:17.000
but eat this and forget about it.

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:20.520
Suzukawa Naoto...

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:23.540
That's a bit too subdued a name for Kitty.

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:27.140
Kitty's so cute...

00:16:27.140 --> 00:16:29.580
I can't believe its name is Suzukawa Naoto.

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:34.280
Somehow I think you're talking about different things.

00:16:34.280 --> 00:16:36.340
Just what is it that Otome loves?

00:16:36.340 --> 00:16:39.280
Otome here! The thing that I love

00:16:39.280 --> 00:16:44.120
is the Kitty-cat silver necklace that the groundskeeping guy was wearing!

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:45.620
What?!

00:16:45.880 --> 00:16:48.840
Looks like you two just completely misunderstood.

00:16:48.840 --> 00:16:52.740
Are you talking about Lulu Christie's Fancy Cat Series?

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:56.720
That's it! I'm in love with that kitty!

00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:59.260
Love you, Kitty!

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:00.840
And for your information,

00:17:00.840 --> 00:17:04.680
there are unique presents for the Special Christmas event,

00:17:04.680 --> 00:17:07.260
and I'm pretty sure that those are included.

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:09.080
I'll do my best!

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:12.000
If it's for Love You, I'll do any-anything!

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:14.260
Love power, Aikatsu!

00:17:14.740 --> 00:17:17.260
Let's train so all four of us can be in the event.

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:29.220
Otome-chan's really going for it.

00:17:29.220 --> 00:17:33.360
In the end, we really racked up a pathetic goose egg.

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:37.200
I'm not sure what that means, but I think I get what you mean.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:39.120
Love You power, right?

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:42.600
Even though romance is forbidden for idols,

00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:44.940
the power of love really is amazing.

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:46.540
Then it'll all be alright.

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:47.790
What do you mean?

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:52.000
It's okay to love as long as it's not all just for one person.

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:55.440
We just need to give everything we've got for all our fans.

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:58.800
That's an idol's Love You power!

00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:00.080
I see.

00:18:11.540 --> 00:18:13.260
I'm really sorry about yesterday.

00:18:13.260 --> 00:18:14.060
It's fine.

00:18:14.520 --> 00:18:17.100
Anyway, you're keeping <i>that</i> a secret, right?

00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:17.820
Yes.

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:21.660
But Suzukawa-san, who are you really?

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:24.920
A band member? Or just the groundskeeper?

00:18:24.920 --> 00:18:26.240
What about you?

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:30.380
Are you the daughter of a bento shop? Are you an idol?

00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:32.840
Both!

00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:35.040
Then I'm both too.

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:38.580
But as long as we're here, I'm the same old groundskeeper.

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:44.360
Isn't it about time for Arisugawa's audition?

00:18:44.360 --> 00:18:46.100
Ah, that's right!

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:33.180
You did it!

00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:34.100
You were the best!

00:21:34.100 --> 00:21:35.320
Nice job.

00:21:35.320 --> 00:21:37.460
It kinda hurts, but I'm happy!

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:38.920
That's just like you, Otome-chan!

00:21:38.920 --> 00:21:41.460
It's my Love You power!

00:21:41.460 --> 00:21:44.440
Now the four of us can be in the
 Special Christmas event together.

00:21:44.440 --> 00:21:47.000
Yep! And I'll get a Kitty!

00:21:47.220 --> 00:21:51.380
It's a good thing that the one you loved wasn't the groundskeeping guy.

00:21:51.380 --> 00:21:53.660
I love that person too!

00:21:53.660 --> 00:21:54.480
Huh?

00:21:54.800 --> 00:21:56.940
I love everyone.

00:21:56.940 --> 00:22:01.980
Having so many things to love makes me really, really happy!

00:22:02.320 --> 00:22:04.940
What incredible positive thinking.

00:22:04.940 --> 00:22:06.980
Love you!

00:22:07.020 --> 00:22:08.720
Ichigo-chan!

00:22:08.720 --> 00:22:10.520
Aoi-chan!

00:22:10.520 --> 00:22:12.260
And Ran-chan!

00:22:12.260 --> 00:22:15.780
I'm in love with every one of you!

00:22:16.080 --> 00:22:17.820
Love is power!

00:22:17.820 --> 00:22:20.840
Love will save the Earth!

00:23:55.510 --> 00:23:57.490
This week's Aikatsu Aphorism.

00:23:58.450 --> 00:24:00.760
What sort of things do you like?

00:24:00.760 --> 00:24:02.220
Well, I like

00:24:02.220 --> 00:24:05.260
nori bento, fried ginger pork, and fried chicken.

00:24:05.260 --> 00:24:07.360
You sure do love your food!

00:24:08.200 --> 00:24:09.620
Love is power!

00:24:10.740 --> 00:24:12.820
The Christmas event is drawing closer.

00:24:12.820 --> 00:24:15.900
Otome-chan, we're in this together, so let's do our best!

00:24:15.900 --> 00:24:17.460
Huh, where'd Otome-chan go?

00:24:17.460 --> 00:24:18.560
Where is she?

00:24:18.560 --> 00:24:20.020
Next time on Aikatsu!

00:24:20.020 --> 00:24:21.840
We wish you a merry Christmas!

00:24:21.840 --> 00:24:25.260
Always passionate, Idol Activities!
